note: Capella product -- its signal does not follow its declared SGN=+1, so the
      FX-to-delay transform is inverted to match Capella's own reference reader.
      Without this the image is mirrored in range.
cphd: skipped 8 vector(s) flagged invalid and 0 with non-finite geometry, of 335149
--no-optimize: unoptimised reference mode.
  correlation peak search  WHOLE zero-padded surface, global maximum,
                           instead of one pixel about the integer peak.
                           This is the only change that can move a number.
  backprojection           single-threaded, ascending cell order. The
                           samples are BITWISE IDENTICAL to a threaded run:
                           each cell accumulates privately over pulses in
                           chronological order and no accumulator is shared,
                           so there is no threading drift here to remove.
                           This half is a reproducibility check, not a fix.
  tracking loop            serial, so window visitation order is fixed.
                           Also cannot change a result; windows are
                           independent.
  Measured cost: the exhaustive search is 1.7-3.2x the optimised one per
  call (2.5x at these defaults), and running serially costs about 4x more
  on eight cores. Single digits overall, not orders of magnitude -- this
  is affordable on a full-scale scene.
  A result from this mode is a second measurement by a slower route, to be
  compared with the first -- not a more trustworthy one. Neither passes a
  null test alone.
warning: --patent-exact selects the master-slave pair the patent
